+ * `duty` is 45·slots/perimeter and `slots` is what the frame can hold). This function knows
+ * only how to cut; the default duty is the shape of the mark, not a policy.
+ *
+ * IT IS GEOMETRY AND NOT A DASH, and the reason is SEGMENT COUNT rather than syntax. WebKit
+ * restarts a dash phase every ~128 segments of a polyline where Chromium dashes the path
+ * whole; a grain-baked ring is 493 segments by construction, so the gauge this replaced
+ * painted 0.228 of the ring in Chromium and 0.921 in WebKit off identical markup, and
+ * decimating the same pose walks it back (123 segments agree). A cut path has no phase for an
+ * engine to restart, so both engines paint the same k, and no board size or grain setting can
+ * push the count past somebody's chunk boundary and regress it.
+ *
+ * It cuts over `poseGeometry` — the memoised, guarded arc-length walk `poseFronts` uses
+ * (ACC-FIVE's cured export) — rather than a scanner of its own: one grammar for every front
